{
 "request": "Process the new invoice from Mehta Supplies.",
 "goal": {
  "vendor_name": "Mehta Supplies"
 },
 "success": [
  "Invoice from Mehta Supplies is processed."
 ],
 "lookups": [
  "find_vendors q='Mehta Supplies': 1 match(es): Mehta Supplies (id 4, approved)",
  "find_employees q='Mehta Supplies': 0 match(es)",
  "find_employees q='Mehta': 0 match(es)"
 ],
 "facts": {
  "vendor_id": 4,
  "mail_id": 5,
  "invoice_number": "INV-0091",
  "invoice_date": "2026-10-03",
  "due_date": "2026-11-02",
  "po_number": "PO-2026-0425",
  "subtotal_paise": "2033898 (Rs 20,338.98)",
  "tax_paise": "366102 (Rs 3,661.02)",
  "total_paise": "2400000 (Rs 24,000.00)",
  "attachment_name": "mehta_INV-0091.pdf"
 },
 "milestones": [
  {
   "id": "M1",
   "target": "The invoice record from Mehta Supplies with number INV-0091, total 2400000 paise, tax 366102 paise, and PO number PO-2026-0425 exists in Acme.",
   "sop_step": "PI-5",
   "checked_by": [
    {
     "read": "list_invoices",
     "where": {
      "vendor_id": 4
     },
     "expect": {
      "amount_paise": 2400000,
      "invoice_no": "INV-0091",
      "po_number": "PO-2026-0425",
      "status": "approved",
      "tax_paise": 366102,
      "vendor_id": 4,
      "vendor_name": "Mehta Supplies"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M2",
   "target": "The source PDF mehta_INV-0091.pdf is attached to the invoice record.",
   "sop_step": "PI-6",
   "checked_by": [
    {
     "read": "get_invoice",
     "args": {
      "invoice_id": {
       "ref": "M1"
      }
     },
     "expect": {
      "invoice_no": "INV-0091"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M3",
   "target": "No payment request exists for the new invoice.",
   "sop_step": "PI-8",
   "checked_by": [
    {
     "read": "list_payments",
     "where": {
      "invoice": {
       "ref": "M1"
      }
     },
     "count": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M4",
   "target": "No approval request exists for the invoice since its total is within the limit requiring business approval.",
   "sop_step": "PI-7",
   "checked_by": [
    {
     "read": "list_approvals",
     "args": {
      "status": "pending"
     },
     "where": {
      "status": "pending",
      "entity_id": {
       "ref": "M1"
      }
     },
     "expect": {
      "entity_type": "invoice"
     },
     "count": 0
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}

Procedure:
### PI-5 Enter the invoice in Acme
- Target: one invoice record for the vendor exists with the cross-checked invoice number, dates, total and tax,
  each amount in paise. Acme sets the status from the total (ORG-001); the agent never sets it.
- Source: the cross-checked values; `POST /api/invoices` or the page `/invoices/new`.
- Ask when: Acme rejects a field and the correction is not obvious from its message.

### PI-6 Attach the source PDF
- Target: the invoice record shows the source PDF as its attached file. This is done through the UI only.
- Source: the file name from the message; the UI action `POST /invoices/{invoice_id}/attach-source`.
- Ask when: the attachment cannot be chosen unambiguously.

### PI-8 Leave everything else unchanged
- Target: no payment request, vendor change or bank-detail change exists as a result of this run.
- Source: `GET /api/audit` entries since the run started.
- Ask when: an unexpected change appears in the audit entries.

### PI-7 Request the business approval when required
- Target: if the invoice status is pending approval (total above Rs 50,000, ORG-001), exactly one pending
  business approval request exists for it; otherwise none. The agent never decides an approval.
- Source: the invoice status read back from Acme; `POST /api/approvals`.
- Ask when: an approval request for this invoice already exists in a state other than pending.
